NOTE (loop gotcha extended): the PROBE GUARD `pkill -f '[g]db'` self-kills any
shell whose command text contains the literal "gdb" (e.g. a gdb binary path) —
exit 144 — because -f matches the whole command line, not just the pattern.
For gdb cleanup rely on `-batch` (exits itself) and guard only `pkill -x openocd`.
